    description:
      "Fear of flying affects an estimated 10–25% of people and is one of the best-treated phobias. In the landmark controlled trial, four sessions of anxiety management followed by four sessions of exposure — to a virtual airplane or an actual airplane — led 93% of both groups to fly within six months versus 20% on the wait list, with gains maintained at twelve months and even through the September 11 attacks. Meta-analyses put virtual-reality exposure on par with in vivo exposure across anxiety disorders, and a 2025 head-to-head trial found ordinary 2D video exposure matched VR at two years. Computer-aided self-administered exposure did as well as therapist-led VR at one-year follow-up.",
    action: "If flying fear limits where you go, book eight sessions of cognitive-behavioral exposure treatment with a clinician who offers VR or graded real-airport exposure, and schedule a real flight within four weeks of the last session while the gains are fresh.",
